{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"id\":\"N315\",\"lines\":\"r-nrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N315.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"Prayer becomes a place toward which one rises. The wording pictures the worshipper moving toward the worship-place.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a place of worship, while قُمْتُمْ is rising toward an undertaking; the place completes the movement.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N315.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلنِّسَآءَ\",\"after\":\"A worship-place can serve a community, here named as women.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a synagogue or prayer-place, and ٱلنِّسَآءَ names a collective group; their link as worshippers and venue is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N315.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"The place of worship points beyond itself to the one worshipped. The verse's prayer-place can be heard as oriented toward Allah.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean a synagogue or worship-place, while ٱللَّهُ names the worshipped; venue and object of worship complete one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N315.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"A worship-place is also a setting in which gratitude may be voiced.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a place of worship, and تَشْكُرُونَ is giving thanks; their connection is the general setting of communal devotion.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N316\",\"lines\":\"-rn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N316.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The selected earth can be pictured as a broad, flat stone. It becomes a working surface touched in the substitute rite.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a broad stone used for pounding, while صَعِيدًا is the earth's surface; both make an image of a usable surface.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N316.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"طَيِّبًا\",\"after\":\"The pounding stone can be linked to a pleasant or fragrant substance.\",\"reason\":\"The rare ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a stone on which perfume is pounded, while طَيِّبًا can mean pleasant or perfuming; the stone is a tool for such a substance.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N317\",\"lines\":\"r--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N317.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِرُءُوسِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The plant's large, head-like spike rises into view. Its shape gives the head a vegetal echo.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a camel-fodder plant with a large spike like the head of a cane, while بِرُءُوسِكُمْ names heads or uppermost parts.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N317.4\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"A fodder plant belongs to the ground surface where it grows.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ here is a plant grazed by camels, and صَعِيدًا is the earth's surface; plant and growing ground are a broad ecological pair.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N318\",\"lines\":\"r--rrn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N318.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The rising becomes the opening posture of worship. The body's movement toward prayer already begins the act of prayer.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is prescribed worship that includes standing, while قُمْتُمْ means rising toward prayer.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N318.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Tayammum is directed toward the prayer for which purification prepares. The substitute rite and the worship it serves form one sequence.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is the prescribed act of worship, while فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ means to aim intentionally; the purification act prepares the worshipper for its goal.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N318.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"The bodily rite is worship offered to Allah. Its standing, bowing, and prostration find their addressee in the divine.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is prescribed worship, and ٱللَّهُ names the worshipped; act and addressee complete one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N318.6\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"Gratitude can be voiced as part of worship.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is ritual devotion, and تَشْكُرُونَ is recognizing and thanking the giver; thanksgiving can form one devotional act within the broader worship.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N319\",\"lines\":\"r-rrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N319.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ءَامَنُوٓا۟\",\"after\":\"The blessing or supplication is directed toward those who trust. Faith names its recipients, and prayer names what is asked or bestowed for them.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ includes supplication or blessing, while ءَامَنُوٓا۟ names those who trust; prayer for believers joins the two.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N319.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَرَافِقِ\",\"after\":\"Prayer as divine mercy sounds beside gentle, easing conduct. Both make kindness the quality heard in the rite.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean mercy, while ٱلْمَرَافِقِ carries gentleness and ease; the senses meet in merciful softness.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N319.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"نِعْمَتَهُۥ\",\"after\":\"The prayer or mercy is itself a favor. The verse's gift is heard as mercy reaching the believers.\",\"reason\":\"The rare divine sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is mercy, and نِعْمَتَهُۥ is favor or blessing; the senses overlap directly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N319.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"Prayer as praise and gratitude meet in recognizing the giver. The final thanks can sound like the answer to blessing.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean supplication, blessing, or praise, while تَشْكُرُونَ means recognizing a favor and praising its giver.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N320\",\"lines\":\"-nr--n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N320.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"لَٰمَسْتُمُ\",\"after\":\"Bodily contact is one way of encountering heat or its hardship.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is to undergo burning heat or comparable distress, while لَٰمَسْتُمُ is bodily touch; contact can expose the body to such heat.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N320.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Finding is an encounter with what is sensed. The rare sense makes that encounter bodily and painful, though the verse negates finding water.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean enduring heat, while تَجِدُوا۟ means finding or perceiving; both can be heard as experiencing something directly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N320.6\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"حَرَجٍ\",\"after\":\"Heat's severity and constriction both name distress.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is suffering the intensity of fire, while حَرَجٍ is constriction or hardship; their shared distress is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N321\",\"lines\":\"-----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N322\",\"lines\":\"nr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N322.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْمَرَافِقِ\",\"after\":\"A snare restrains, while facility and gentle action ease movement.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a trap set to catch prey, while ٱلْمَرَافِقِ evokes ease and deftness; the two pull in opposite directions.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N322.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Both senses involve setting an aim. The trap is laid toward its quarry, just as tayammum is intentionally directed toward its medium.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean a trap set for birds or other prey, while فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ means to aim intentionally at something.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N323\",\"lines\":\"nr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N323.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْكَعْبَيْنِ\",\"after\":\"The back or tail base and the ankle are bodily landmarks.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ names the middle back or the sides of the tail base, while ٱلْكَعْبَيْنِ names protruding ankle bones; the relation is anatomical but general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N323.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"جُنُبًا\",\"after\":\"The rare word names the body's flank, and junub names a state associated with being at the side or apart. The bodily-side image is repeated within the verse's impurity condition.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean the back's middle or the sides near the tail, while جُنُبًا means the body's side or a thing's adjacent region.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N324\",\"lines\":\"-----r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N324.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"after\":\"The second horse is the one that arrives after the leader. جَآءَ can therefore sound as an arrival within a sequence.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is the horse that follows the leader in a race, while جَآءَ means coming or arriving; both evoke arrival, with the rare sense adding order.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N325\",\"lines\":\"-nrr-n\"}\n{\"id\":\"N325.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلنِّسَآءَ\",\"after\":\"A synagogue or worship-place serves the people who gather there, including women.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean a Jewish temple or synagogue, while ٱلنِّسَآءَ names a community of women; venue and worshippers form a general pair.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N325.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The worship-place is a destination toward which the worshipper aims. The substitute purification turns the body toward the worship it prepares for.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a place of worship, while فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ means to aim intentionally; the aimed rite and worship-place complement one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N325.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱللَّهُ\",\"after\":\"A temple points to the one worshipped there. The place and Allah form the setting and object of devotion.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean a Jewish place of worship, while ٱللَّهُ names the worshipped; venue and object of worship meet directly.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N325.6\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَشْكُرُونَ\",\"after\":\"A place of worship can also be a place where thanks are offered.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ is a worship-place, and تَشْكُرُونَ is giving thanks; the connection is a general devotional setting.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N326\",\"lines\":\"-r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N326.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ\",\"target_ar\":\"طَيِّبًا\",\"after\":\"The broad stone is a tool for pounding what is fragrant or pleasant. The clean, wholesome surface is heard beside the pleasant substance made on such a stone.\",\"reason\":\"ٱلصَّلَوٰةِ can mean a broad stone on which perfume is pounded, while طَيِّبًا means pleasant, clean, or good; the stone is a tool for a pleasant substance.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N327\",\"lines\":\"-----\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328\",\"lines\":\"-rrrnrr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Washing and wiping are paired modes of purification. The verse moves from one contact with water to a lighter pass over the head.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ includes washing water or a washing medium, while وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ means passing a hand over something; the actions complement each other.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"بِرُءُوسِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The washing place or washing medium is linked to the head it serves. The head becomes a concrete bodily object of cleansing.\",\"reason\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ can carry the sense of water or a place used for washing the head, while بِرُءُوسِكُمْ names the head.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱطَّهَّرُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Washing is one stage by which a person becomes purified. The later command gathers the bodily cleansing into a fuller reset.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ is washing water, medium, or place, while فَٱطَّهَّرُوا۟ means to purify oneself; washing serves the purification.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328.5\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"ٱلْغَآئِطِ\",\"after\":\"A washing-place can be pictured in a low hollow.\",\"reason\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ can mean a place for washing, while ٱلْغَآئِطِ is low or hollow terrain; both name a place, though the link is general.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"مَآءً\",\"after\":\"The wash-medium is water itself. The missing water is the very substance carried by the rare sense of washing.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ includes the water used for washing, while مَآءً names water.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N328.7\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"Washing and wiping are two ways to cleanse. The verse places the lighter wiping action beside the wash-medium's broader cleansing sense.\",\"reason\":\"فَٱغْسِلُوا۟ can mean the water or material used in washing, while فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ means wiping over a surface; the modes complement one another.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N329\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N330\",\"lines\":\"-rr-rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N330.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"جُنُبًا\",\"after\":\"Face-to-face confrontation turns the front toward another, while the flank is the side. The verse's face and junub can be heard as opposed bodily orientations.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is facing someone directly, while جُنُبًا names the body's side or flank.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N330.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The face-to-face meeting is an encounter. The verb for finding makes the direct meeting sound as something actually met or perceived.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can carry the sense of confronting someone, while تَجِدُوا۟ means to encounter or perceive something.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N330.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The face turns toward what it confronts. Tayammum also names a directed aim, so both senses draw the body toward a target.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is face-to-face orientation, while فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ means aiming intentionally at something.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N330.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The face meets the face of the earth. The pairing evokes the worshipper's bodily orientation toward the ground used in the substitute rite.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean confronting or facing someone, while صَعِيدًا is the earth's surface, its face; together they make an image of a face meeting a surface.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N331\",\"lines\":\"rr---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N331.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Standing among the foremost involves authority and agency. The hand's power is one means by which a leader exercises that standing.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is social prominence or high rank, while وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ can mean hands or power; power is an instrument of rank.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N331.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِرُءُوسِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The prominent person is the head of a group. Social precedence and the head as the top or leader converge in one image.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean the prominent people or leaders, while بِرُءُوسِكُمْ names heads or the highest parts; both carry the image of leadership.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N332\",\"lines\":\"r---r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N332.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"The face of the day is its first stretch, when people rise into their tasks. The morning's opening and the body's rising meet in an image of beginnings.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is the day's early hours, while قُمْتُمْ means rising toward an undertaking.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N332.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِوُجُوهِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Both uses of face can name what is foremost or facing outward. The first hours of the day and the fronts of the body share that image of a face.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean the beginning or face of the day, while بِوُجُوهِكُمْ names faces or forward-facing sides.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333\",\"lines\":\"n-nrr-nn\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"قُمْتُمْ\",\"after\":\"Rising toward prayer begins an action that can be performed in its proper order.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is the right course or proper arrangement of an affair, while قُمْتُمْ is rising toward prayer; the link is a general one of ordered preparation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333.3\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِرُءُوسِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The head can be the leading part of an affair's proper arrangement.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean the right direction or proper order of a matter, while بِرُءُوسِكُمْ names the head or top; the head can mark a beginning, but the link is broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The feet carry a person along a course. The phrase can picture the proper way made bodily through walking.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is the right way or proper direction, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ evokes walking on feet.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"مَّرْضَىٰٓ\",\"after\":\"The right order of an affair stands against a departure from health and balance. The verse's proper way and illness pull toward soundness and away from it.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean the correct course or arrangement, while مَّرْضَىٰٓ names illness as a departure from health.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333.7\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The proper face of an affair can be heard beside the face or surface of the earth.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is the right direction of a matter, while صَعِيدًا is the earth's surface; the shared face-image is suggestive but broad.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N333.8\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"A wiping action can be carried out in its proper manner.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean the proper order of an affair, while فَٱمْسَحُوا۟ is the act of wiping; the prescribed action fits the order only generally.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N334\",\"lines\":\"-n-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N334.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Age can affect how a person walks on their legs.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is entering old age, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ evokes walking on legs; age and gait have a general bodily relation.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N335\",\"lines\":\"-r-r--r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N335.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Hands lead the birth in the rare image, and hands are later named as the body's working parts. The rite recalls the same limbs that first emerged.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is a birth in which the hands emerge first, while وَأَيْدِيَكُمْ names the hands as body parts.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N335.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"complement\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ\",\"after\":\"Hands emerge first in the birth image; legs later carry the growing child. The two senses make a sequence from first arrival to walking.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean a birth in which hands appear first, while وَأَرْجُلَكُمْ evokes walking on legs; the limbs mark complementary stages.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N335.7\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَأَيْدِيكُم\",\"after\":\"The hands that lead the birth image reappear as hands used in the substitute rite. Their first emergence is echoed in their later ritual use.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is a birth with hands emerging first, while وَأَيْدِيكُم names the hands wiped in tayammum.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N336\",\"lines\":\"---\"}\n{\"id\":\"N337\",\"lines\":\"rr-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N337.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟\",\"after\":\"The fruit is deliberately inclined into a chosen position. That physical turning gives an image to the intentional aiming named by tayammum.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is digging under a fruit to incline it, while فَتَيَمَّمُوا۟ means intentionally aiming at something.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N337.2\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The plant is tilted by digging beneath the ground surface. The verse's selected earth can be pictured as the surface around which that positioning happens.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean digging below a cucumber or melon to lay it at an angle, while صَعِيدًا is the earth's surface; the two make a grounded image of positioning.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N338\",\"lines\":\"nn-rr\"}\n{\"id\":\"N338.1\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"A blow and a wipe are contrasting ways of touching the face, one forceful and one gentle.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is striking someone's face, while وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ is passing a hand over a surface; the contact modes oppose each other in force.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N338.2\",\"verdict\":\"note\",\"relation\":\"same\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"تَجِدُوا۟\",\"after\":\"A blow is an event one encounters or experiences.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean striking someone in the face, while تَجِدُوا۟ means finding or experiencing; the blow is something encountered.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N338.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"صَعِيدًا\",\"after\":\"The struck face meets the face of the earth. The image turns the rite's contact with the earth into a forceful echo of prostration.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is a blow to the face, while صَعِيدًا is the earth's surface; together they picture a face striking the ground.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N338.5\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِوُجُوهِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The face is the part that receives the blow. The second face-word names the very surface implicated in the rare sense.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean striking someone in the face, while بِوُجُوهِكُمْ names the face; the target is the body part struck.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N339\",\"lines\":\"--r-\"}\n{\"id\":\"N339.3\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"opposite\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"جَآءَ\",\"after\":\"جَآءَ names coming into presence; the rare sense sends the one who came back away. Arrival meets refusal at the threshold.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is turning away someone who comes, while جَآءَ means to come or arrive; sending back opposes arrival.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N340\",\"lines\":\"r--r-r\"}\n{\"id\":\"N340.1\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"وَٱمْسَحُوا۟\",\"after\":\"A wipe passes over one surface of a two-sided object. The rare sense supplies the two faces, and the verb supplies the contact with one of them.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean a two-faced cloak or object, while وَٱمْسَحُوا۟ means wiping over a surface; the wiped face is one part of the two-sided object.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N340.4\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"part\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"جُنُبًا\",\"after\":\"A side is one face of a two-sided object. The verse's bodily side can be heard beside the object's paired faces.\",\"reason\":\"The rare sense of وُجُوهَكُمْ is a two-faced object or person, while جُنُبًا names a side or flank; a side is one aspect of a two-sided form.\"}\n{\"id\":\"N340.6\",\"verdict\":\"reading\",\"relation\":\"image\",\"focus_ar\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ\",\"target_ar\":\"بِوُجُوهِكُمْ\",\"after\":\"The washed face is the public, outward surface. Beside the rare two-faced person whose outside conflicts with the heart, it invites an image of outward cleansing beside inward truth.\",\"reason\":\"وُجُوهَكُمْ can mean a person whose outward face differs from the heart, while بِوُجُوهِكُمْ names the face or forward side; the pair makes an image of outer face and hidden interior.\"}"}}
